@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] updater-verifies-before-install
The updater installs only an APK whose SHA-256 matches `latest.json` and whose
`versionCode` is higher than the installed one; a mismatch is an error and nothing is
installed. Installation goes through Android's own installer and its approval.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] updater-asks-only-its-server
Updates come only from the configured server's `/download/latest.json` (Pully Staging:
`/download/staging/latest.json`, android `android-staging-channel`) and the APK it names,
with saved compatibility Access headers, or path-confined baked staging Access
headers in the GitHub workspace (Tavi25Oct2026). No third-party update
service or library is in the path.
The manifest MUST name a binary APK URL rather than the `/download` HTML page.
Source: Tavi's 22 Oct 2026 download-page and removed direct-APK decision.
Anonymous Explore MUST NOT start configured private-server update checks, downloads or
installation from an old notification. The independently scoped built-in staging
channel MAY update without private-server authority (Tavi25Oct2026). A late check for
a replaced configured source MUST NOT change its replacement's state.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 signed-out public browsing and separate entry-authority plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] updater-baked-access-is-checked-per-hop
Baked Access headers MUST be recomputed for every manifest, history and APK redirect.
Only the exact built-in HTTPS staging origin and /download/staging/* paths MAY receive
them; forbidden same-origin paths, including /api/personal/*, /api/rpc and /workspace/*,
MUST receive none of that baked credential. Saved ExistingServer credentials retain
their same-origin compatibility behavior. Source: Tavi's 25 Oct 2026 staging-only
credential decision and confirmed review finding 6.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] updater-source-is-independent-of-workspace-mount
Application startup, background checks, foreground checks, notification downloads and
history requests MUST share one effective update configuration. Explore and GitHub
MUST select built-in staging when its scoped download credential is available, even
with no mounted workspace and a saved custom server; they MUST NOT read or overwrite
that saved compatibility configuration or require a personal bearer. Explicit
ExistingServer MUST select the saved server and saved Access credentials independently
of any binding. Other anonymous configurations MUST remain unavailable. Saved server
or Access-token changes MUST resync periodic work; ownership mount/retirement and
notification preference changes MUST also resync it. Source: Tavi's 25 Oct 2026
one-login updater decision and confirmed review finding 7.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] updater-remembers-the-offer
The phone remembers the last offer, so the update screen is there before the server
answers again, and the offer goes once the server has nothing newer (rule 104).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] updater-notifies-once
A new version is told in a notification while the app is closed, once per version
(rule 104).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] updater-update-pulls-command
Update Pully in Commands asks the server at once and starts the update, or says this is
the newest version (rule 104).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] updater-installation-recovers
An update MUST persist its own installer session and target version before handing bytes
to Android. Only callbacks for that session MAY change its result. Confirmation MUST be
opened by the resumed activity and remain available when the reader returns. Interrupted
or expired installs MUST offer retry, and only the installed package version MAY settle
success. Source: Tavi, 21 Oct 2026, updates stuck at installing or downloading; rule 63.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] past-versions-install-beside
A past version installs only from the configured server's channel-specific history
(`/download/past/` for stable, `/download/staging/past/` for staging), only when
its SHA-256 matches `index.json`, and only as its own `com.octaviantocan.pulls.v*`
package: the installer is told the package name, so a past build can never replace
this app. Its versionCode is offset so no update is ever offered to it.
The canonical namespace follows Tavi's 22 Oct 2026 download-page decision; existing
read-only history aliases MAY remain for older installed clients.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] past-versions-get-the-server-at-launch
A past version gets the server address and Access token only in the explicit intent
that opens it, and only when its package is signed with this app's key; nothing else
exposes them to other apps. Its activity is behind a signature permission, so no other
app can open it and point it at another server.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] github-workspace-retains-staging-updates
The GitHub workspace MUST run the existing foreground/resume check, update gate,
verified APK download and installer flow without a legacy server login. Staging
manifest/APK requests MUST use /download/staging/* and only that built-in origin's
baked Access credential. Background update readiness MUST not depend on ExistingServer
when that scoped staging configuration is available. Personal login/read transport
MUST remain separate and receive no Access headers. Source: Tavi25Oct2026, production
update behavior under one GitHub login and the approved staging-only APK token.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] staging-history-does-not-adopt-stable-builds
Past versions MUST use the installed app's UPDATE_CHANNEL for its index, APK paths and
local index cache. Staging MUST NOT display or install stable history as staging; an
empty published staging index MUST show the existing truthful empty state. Historical
backfill is outside this delivery. Source: Tavi25Oct2026, full Settings/update flow and
the confirmed staging publisher with no historical APKs.
